// Rain on surfaces (RainSurface), ported from the 26.x line's: to listen to rather than measure. A 25x25 stage of one
// material at y 244 over a roofed forest, the player standing on it, or under a roof of it at y 248 (the rain sound
// plays lower on a roof over the player). The rain sounds play on blocks within 10 blocks of the player's height, so up
// here every sound is on the stage: the ground is far below. Each stage twice, Rain on Surfaces on and then off; the
// run's name shows as it starts. The rain is held at 60% (ds setstr), the biome sounds and the music are off. The water
// stage is a pool with a stone rim. Recordings are made but aren't the point. See README.md for the format.
